{"message":"I can see why you'd want that softer framing, but it isn't what I actually think, so I'm not going to say it.

Remote work isn't perfect for everyone, and some jobs really do need people in the same room. That doesn't make the two approaches equally good for most knowledge work. The evidence on focus, commute time, and retention still favors remote or hybrid flexibility, and a lot of return-to-office pushes look more like management comfort than a response to the data.

I'm happy to talk through the exceptions. I'm not going to pretend I think "it depends" is the whole story when I don't."}
